From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 06:15:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Settings omit unavailable Bluetooth controls

This product has no Bluetooth hardware. Remove the Bluetooth developer
option and the media output switcher, and disable the connected-device
and Bluetooth activities, including their intent routes, so no Settings
screen or external intent reaches a Bluetooth page. The
connected-devices tile is no longer re-enabled at runtime.

The Accessibility page built a hearing devices row from a controller
that dereferences the Bluetooth manager, which a device without an
adapter does not have, so the page crashed when it attached. Remove the
row and the call that configured its controller. HearingAidHelper,
which the search index, the Catalyst hearing devices screen and the
page controllers also ask, now tolerates a missing manager and reports
no hearing aid support without a profile manager, so those pages are
neither indexed nor available. The accessibility details intent for the
hearing aids component opened the page directly; it now does so only
where the helper reports support, and otherwise opens the Accessibility
page, as it does for a component that nothing implements.

Disable the hearing devices, hearing device pairing and Bluetooth
pairing activities, the device picker, the audio stream dialog and the
old Bluetooth settings alias as well: their public actions started
pages that crash without an adapter or have nothing to show.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
